    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5796" root="جسر" body-key="j">
    
      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تجاسر</span></b> : see 1, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>He
stretched himself up, and raised his head.</i> (K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تجاسر لَهُ بِالعَصَا</span> <i>He put himself in motion to
him</i> (En-Nawádir, K) <i>with the staff,</i> or <i>stick.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تجاسروا</span> <i>They acted with mutual daring</i>
or <i>courage</i> or <i>boldness.</i> (KL.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <i>They journeyed</i>
[app. <i>with boldness,</i> or <i>emulating one another in boldness</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الخَيْلُ تَجَاسَرُ بِالكُمَاةِ</span> [for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتَجَاسَرُ</span>]
(tropical:)  <i>The horses convey the brave armed men away,</i>
or <i>along,</i> or <i>across.</i> (A.)

